1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:03,793
You have probably heard that avocado is a healthy fat.

2
00:00:04,548 --> 00:00:09,022
That is true, and it is also the least interesting thing about it.

3
00:00:09,777 --> 00:00:16,297
Because the most powerful thing an avocado does has almost nothing to do with the avocado itself.

4
00:00:17,052 --> 00:00:20,405
It has to do with whatever else is on your plate.

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,985
Here is the claim I want to prove to you.

6
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:32,183
If you eat a large, colorful salad with a fat free dressing, you are throwing away most of the nutrition in it.

7
00:00:32,938 --> 00:00:34,048
Not some of it.

8
00:00:34,804 --> 00:00:35,650
Most of it.

9
00:00:36,405 --> 00:00:37,977
Let's follow the food.

10
00:00:38,732 --> 00:00:46,307
An avocado is roughly fifteen percent fat, and most of that is oleic acid, the same fat that dominates olive oil.

11
00:00:47,062 --> 00:00:51,206
It also carries a large amount of fiber, and almost no sugar.

12
00:00:51,961 --> 00:00:55,512
In the stomach, that fat does something immediately.

13
00:00:56,267 --> 00:00:58,169
Fat slows gastric emptying.

14
00:00:58,924 --> 00:01:07,752
The stomach releases its contents into the intestine more gradually, which is part of why avocado is unusually filling for its size.

15
00:01:08,508 --> 00:01:13,905
Then the mixture reaches the duodenum, the first section of the small intestine.

16
00:01:14,661 --> 00:01:19,003
And fat arriving here triggers a hormone called cholecystokinin.

17
00:01:19,758 --> 00:01:21,792
That hormone does two things.

18
00:01:22,547 --> 00:01:27,021
It signals the gallbladder to contract, squeezing out stored bile.

19
00:01:27,776 --> 00:01:33,570
And it tells the pancreas to release lipase, the enzyme that cuts fat molecules apart.

20
00:01:34,325 --> 00:01:39,855
Now watch what bile actually does, because this is the center of the entire video.

21
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:42,908
Bile salts are unusual molecules.

22
00:01:43,663 --> 00:01:46,290
One end of them is attracted to water.

23
00:01:47,045 --> 00:01:49,409
The other end is attracted to fat.

24
00:01:50,164 --> 00:01:58,332
When they meet fat droplets in your intestine, they surround them and break them into microscopic spheres called micelles.

25
00:01:59,087 --> 00:02:03,628
Water loving surface on the outside, fat loving core on the inside.

26
00:02:04,383 --> 00:02:06,614
A micelle is a delivery vehicle.

27
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:16,264
And it is the only way a fat soluble molecule can cross the watery layer lining your intestinal wall and reach the cells that absorb.

28
00:02:17,019 --> 00:02:19,382
Here is where your salad comes in.

29
00:02:20,137 --> 00:02:23,029
The color in vegetables is not decoration.

30
00:02:23,784 --> 00:02:29,973
Carotenoids are the pigments that make carrots orange, tomatoes red, and spinach deep green.

31
00:02:30,728 --> 00:02:31,772
Beta carotene.

32
00:02:32,528 --> 00:02:33,242
Lycopene.

33
00:02:33,997 --> 00:02:34,579
Lutein.

34
00:02:35,334 --> 00:02:37,632
Every one of them is fat soluble.

35
00:02:38,387 --> 00:02:40,685
They refuse to dissolve in water.

36
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:47,497
So if you eat a salad with no fat on it, there are no micelles waiting for those pigments.

37
00:02:48,252 --> 00:02:55,695
They travel the length of your intestine, past every absorbing cell, and leave your body essentially untouched.

38
00:02:56,450 --> 00:02:57,429
You ate them.

39
00:02:58,184 --> 00:02:59,887
You never absorbed them.

40
00:03:00,643 --> 00:03:03,798
Add avocado, and the entire situation changes.

41
00:03:04,553 --> 00:03:14,832
Its fat drives bile release, micelles form, and the carotenoids from every other food on that plate load into them and get carried to the intestinal wall.

42
00:03:15,587 --> 00:03:20,457
Inside the absorbing cell, something happens that surprises most people.

43
00:03:21,213 --> 00:03:27,996
These fats and pigments are not sent straight to the liver through the bloodstream, the way sugar is.

44
00:03:28,751 --> 00:03:37,051
They are packed into large particles called chylomicrons, and those particles are too big to squeeze into a blood capillary.

45
00:03:37,806 --> 00:03:46,635
So they enter the lymphatic system instead, travel up through your chest, and only then empty into your bloodstream near your heart.

46
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:51,732
Your salad takes a completely different route through your body.

47
00:03:52,487 --> 00:03:54,587
So what does the evidence say?

48
00:03:55,342 --> 00:03:57,310
This one is unusually clear.

49
00:03:58,065 --> 00:04:08,212
In controlled human trials, adding fresh avocado to a salad increased beta carotene absorption several fold, and lutein absorption rose sharply as well.

50
00:04:08,967 --> 00:04:14,761
When avocado was added to a tomato salsa, lycopene absorption increased substantially.

51
00:04:15,516 --> 00:04:25,532
Adding avocado oil on its own produced a similar effect, which tells us the mechanism really is the fat, and not something exotic hidden in the fruit.

52
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:37,028
On the gut itself, the fiber in avocado does shift the bacterial community and increases fat excretion in stool, and that has been measured in randomized trials.

53
00:04:37,783 --> 00:04:39,223
But be careful here.

54
00:04:39,978 --> 00:04:43,002
Those changes are real, and they are modest.

55
00:04:43,757 --> 00:04:49,287
Anyone promising you a transformed microbiome from one fruit is selling something.

56
00:04:50,042 --> 00:04:51,152
So, four rules.

57
00:04:51,907 --> 00:04:52,291
One.

58
00:04:53,046 --> 00:04:57,389
Do not eat avocado alone if you can eat it alongside vegetables.

59
00:04:58,144 --> 00:05:00,969
Its real value is unlocked next to color.

60
00:05:01,724 --> 00:05:02,109
Two.

61
00:05:02,864 --> 00:05:04,898
Stop using fat free dressing.

62
00:05:05,653 --> 00:05:08,940
It is the most wasteful habit in healthy eating.

63
00:05:09,695 --> 00:05:15,225
A fat free dressing on a carotenoid rich salad discards most of what you paid for.

64
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:16,496
Three.

65
00:05:17,251 --> 00:05:21,330
Do not scrape the flesh clean and throw the dark layer away.

66
00:05:22,085 --> 00:05:29,858
The dark green flesh immediately under the peel carries the highest concentration of carotenoids in the whole fruit.

67
00:05:30,613 --> 00:05:31,063
Four.

68
00:05:31,818 --> 00:05:33,324
You do not need much.

69
00:05:34,079 --> 00:05:40,401
A modest amount of fat, in the range of half an avocado, is enough to drive micelle formation.

70
00:05:41,156 --> 00:05:44,443
This is not an argument for eating four of them.

71
00:05:45,198 --> 00:05:46,374
Two quick notes.

72
00:05:47,129 --> 00:05:52,527
Avocado is energy dense, so if you are managing your weight, the amount matters.

73
00:05:53,282 --> 00:06:00,263
And if you have a latex allergy, avocado is one of the fruits that can cross react, so be aware of that.

74
00:06:01,018 --> 00:06:03,844
None of this was really about an avocado.

75
00:06:04,599 --> 00:06:13,955
It was about a delivery vehicle built out of bile, and the simple fact that a nutrient you do not absorb was never really a nutrient at all.

76
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:17,469
So which molecule should we follow next?

77
00:06:18,224 --> 00:06:23,820
Write a food and an organ in the comments, and we will take it apart, cell by cell.

